                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Very recommendable precision platformer with creative and fun to gain achievements for a few bucks. \n\nI really enjoyed the main menu, as many games tend to have clunky main menus especially on Steam Deck. This worked great, though!\n\nNever a big fan of \"die 1000 timew\"-achievements, as they mostly contain just pointless grinding. If you're going for 100%, you're gonna get it anyway, but if you're like me and just want to play until you have a good amount of achievements, seen everything the game has to offer and are content with finishing it, achievements like those are annoying. \nBesides that one, the achievements are well done.\n\nI liked the 16 levels-theme the game is going for.\n\nIt could be shown more clearly, what the mode in the game is you have to get the C/B/A/A++ for the achievements for, as there are 16 levels and then two packs, one with 3 levels and one with 7. You can have a runthrough of all of these 3 packs. You only get a mark in 2 of those packs, which is confusing, and also you can be confused which one needs to be the one for the achievements. So that's a confusing aspect.\n\nAnother thing I had noticed, after finishing a run you can either say retry or go to main menu. My controls (up & down) were always reserved there - in the main menu this never happened. Little thing to fix\n\nBut yeah, for 2,39€ the game is a great little platformer you could either spend like 2-5 hours in for some fun time and achievements, or like 100s of hours as it's also great for speedrunning and seems to have integrated leaderboards for every level.",
